---
layout: changelog
title: "See why every change was made with reasons in Activity"
date: 2026-11-12
cover: /images/blog/announcing-activity-reasons/cover.avif
tags: console, mcp, cli, security
---

Your project's Activity tab now shows why each change was made. A new Reason column sits next to every event, and the event's details show the full text, so reviewing what an AI agent or a script changed takes a glance.

- **The Appwrite MCP server** asks the AI agent for a one-line reason with every change it makes, and refuses a change without one.
- **The Appwrite CLI** takes a reason for any command, either as a flag or as an environment variable that covers a whole CI job.
- **Your own code** can send a reason with any API request, including from the server SDKs.

A reason is one line of up to 256 characters, in any language. Reasons are available on Appwrite Cloud today.

